+# Task 5b: profiles and specificity, using validated emitted records
+
+Own lens_fitting/profiles.py, scripts/lens_profiles.py, tests/test_lens_profiles.py, and a narrow prose-kind extension in scripts/live_lens_atlas.py. Source only; no checkpoint, MLX, network or generation. Parent supplies the final Task5a commit before dispatch. Use the persistent worktree and primary virtualenv with PYTHONPATH=src; you are not alone, preserve other edits. Commit explicit paths and a task-5b-report.md here. No subagents, merges, pushes or full suite. Native model slots remain coordinated by parent.
+
+Read requirements sections2,3.5,3.6,5,14, this plan, artifacts.py, validation.py, Jacobian require_self_check and plan verification, reviewed replay.py, prose.py, existing atlas and live_lens records/session. Do not invent a new summary, primary layer, metric or experiment.
+
+## Output rows
+
+One JSON per named model/domain/kind lens set, plus a standalone HTML page. Every numerical row is separated by episode, layer, episode kind, span and (for foreknowledge) horizon1/4/8. Do not pool tokens across episodes or layers. Every row carries numerator/denominator n and explicit target/span roles. Use all nonfinal residual layers; include final identity only as the base-rate control. No layer chosen as primary.
+
+Foreknowledge scores only actual emitted token events. Rank rows identify source position t and horizon h; their target coordinate is t+h. Pair every eligible nonfinal rank with the FINAL row for the same episode, turn, source position, target position/token ID and horizon. Missing/duplicate/extra pairs are a hard failure, not silently filtered; n must match. Report exact share ranked<=10 and corresponding final share on every row. A zero denominator is null, not zero. Preserve the pilot definition of emitted target span: agentic note/call as the legacy helper determines after the emitted event; chat remains chat; prose always continuation. Identify span_role='emitted_target'. EOS follows the producer's recorded convention. Never score the descriptive authored tail as emitted tokens.
+
+Prompt agreement uses reading position t where t+1 remains inside the authored/rendered prompt; compare layer top1 to recorded prompt_ids[t+1]. Label by source prompt-position span, matching the existing atlas; make span_role explicit so source/target span is not implied to be the same at boundaries. For prose use the raw authored prompt positions. Verify tokenizer offset labels align with exact prompt IDs; no retokenization fallback. A prompt/emission boundary never becomes prompt agreement.
+
+Regression horizon1 rows are marked biased_by_construction and excluded from the reading rule. Do not suppress their data. Jacobian interpretive eligibility uses each layer's recorded map_check verdict; concept/output hooks remain unchanged and inconclusive until separately specified. No new refit logic. If any interpretive rule is emitted, it must name the requirement's exact reference horizon and its eligibility, and must not conflate h1, h4 and h8. Prefer report the pre-registered rows and eligibility clearly rather than infer an unsupported aggregate conclusion. Failed/inconclusive map rows remain visible with status.
+
+Specificity must label lens training domain and evaluation material separately: agentic lens on pilot agentic episodes and on held-prose continuations; prose lens on both. Chat pilot rows remain visible as chat evaluation, not a third fitted domain. State the prose held-set ridge-selection overlap from§14, and distinguish disjoint pilot generalisation. Missing cross-read cells are explicitly unavailable, not absent from the table or replaced with chat. No new download or authored-text foreknowledge.
+
+## Evidence gates and artifacts
+
+Profile CLI requires source-bound instrument self-check evidence and exact hosted-pilot replay identity evidence BEFORE it reads/summarizes scientific records. Validate the actual files and their hashes, not a supplied success boolean. Reuse existing pure require_self_check(plan, proof) with a verified frozen plan and snapshot identity. For a Jacobian lens, bind plan hash to its fitted sidecar and carry per-layer validation. For regression/hosted comparisons, an independently passed cached/reference proof on the same model snapshot establishes the shared instrument path; state that it is not a claim of regression Jacobian map agreement. Keep evidence provenance explicit.
+
+Identity evidence is Task4 identity.json plus its real source/output atlases and replay metadata/complete records. Recompute exact JSON equality and verify referenced hashes and output record set. Do not accept a forged exact_json_equal flag alone, a synthetic fixture passed as native production proof, or a sidecar whose snapshot/lens identity differs from the data. Tests may construct explicit tiny fixtures without claiming actual native acceptance.
+
+Task4 deliberately keeps historical manifest.json bytes for legacy identity; it is not the authority for the new output record hashes or lens. New replay provenance is replay-manifest.json and replay-complete.json: consume those for current lens/domain/layers/snapshot and actual output hashes, while using historical episode metadata only for labels/kind/difficulty. Verify hash chains with existing read_source/read_record and complete output set before aggregation. Original capture sets from Task5a use their own accepted/dropped manifest and completion contract; only accepted root episodes may enter prose profiles. Read the final Task5a API before choosing this adapter.
+
+Output identity binds selected lens NPZ/sidecar, current replay/capture records, model snapshot, corpus/evaluation metadata, identity and self-check files, source commit, metric conventions and all exclusions. Use exclusive output creation, allow_nan=False, no silent overwrite, no automatic scientific execution during import or plan preparation. Hash/revalidate consumed files; a changed input must fail closed. Avoid loading the NPZ matrices just to summarize if an exact file hash/sidecar and validated replay provenance suffice. No model is needed for summaries.
+
+## Legacy compatibility and page
+
+The current legacy emitted_span returns note for all non-chat kinds. Add only a prose branch returning continuation, and raw-prose prompt span support where needed. Preserve all original agentic/chat atlas values exactly; use the parent's saved offline pilot control or actual original records and the cached tokenizer, not a second copy of the algorithm. Do not change original atlas.json/records. Legacy identity continues to use the actual script, whose updated SHA is recorded.
+
+The new page shows curves over all nonfinal layers and each row's final base-rate horizontal line. Filters select lens set, episode, kind, span and horizon/summary; there is no implicit pooled default. State n, the regression-h1 limitation, validation status and unavailable cross-read cells. Standalone HTML/CSS/SVG/JS, no remote CDN; keyboard-usable controls, escaped text and embedded JSON safe against script termination. Exported JSON is the authoritative data. No fabricated example scientific readings.
+
+Tests should be small independently calculable fixtures: changing one episode cannot change another's row; same rank with a different horizon/turn/target cannot pair; missing/duplicate final pairs fail; regression h1 excluded but retained; prose uses own base rate; authored descriptive tail never enters ranks; prompt boundary excluded; dropped prose excluded; malformed/changed evidence refused before aggregation; changed current lens/source hashes refused; actual legacy pilot output unchanged by prose support. Confirm zero MLX imports and pure CLI behavior. Report executed evidence separately from the still-pending native scientific gates.
